  "details": "The kernel packages contain the Linux kernel, the core of any Linux operating system.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * kernel: USB: serial: io_ti: fix heap overflow in get_manuf_info() (CVE-2026-53196)\n  * kernel: net/iucv: fix use-after-free of a severed iucv_path (CVE-2026-68140)\n  * kernel: sctp: avoid auth_enable sysctl UAF during netns teardown (CVE-2026-68162)\n  * kernel: s390/zcrypt: Validate length for CCA AES cipher key requests (CVE-2026-68452)\n  * kernel: s390/zcrypt: Validate length for CCA ECC private key requests (CVE-2026-68451)\n  * kernel: sunrpc: pin svc_xprt across the asynchronous TLS handshake callback (CVE-2026-72222)\n  * kernel: sunrpc: wait for in-flight TLS handshake callback when cancel loses race (CVE-2026-72221)\n  * kernel: nvmet-tcp: check return value of nvmet_tcp_set_queue_sock (CVE-2026-74385)\n  * kernel: sctp: keep chunk->transport in step with the list it is queued on (CVE-2026-74588)\n  * kernel: sctp: clear new_transport when removing a peer (CVE-2026-74586)\n  * kernel: sctp: validate cookie AUTH state before use (CVE-2026-74752)\n  * kernel: mptcp: options: reset DSS fields in case of unexpected size (CVE-2026-80586)\n  * kernel: s390/vfio_ccw: Cancel existing workqueues (CVE-2026-80553)\n  * kernel: powerpc/pseries: papr-phy-attest - validate cmd.length, plug mem leak (CVE-2026-80571)\n  * kernel: s390/qeth: validate user buffer length in SNMP and ARP query ioctls (CVE-2026-80584)\n  * kernel: ipv6: fix use-after-free in ip6_finish_output2() (CVE-2026-80792)\n  * kernel: net/smc: fix use-after-free of the LLC qentry in smc_llc_srv_add_link() (CVE-2026-80981)\n  * kernel: smb: client: fix OOB read/write from unvalidated DataOffset in coalesce_t2() (CVE-2026-89633)\n  * kernel: sctp: stop processing a packet once its association is deleted (CVE-2026-89479)\n  * kernel: s390/vfio-ap: Fix missing lock required to access list of ap_matrix_mdev objects (CVE-2026-89956)\n  * kernel: ALSA: seq: midi: Serialize input teardown with event_input (CVE-2026-90207)\n  * kernel: ALSA: pcm: Serialize PCM mmap with buffer reallocation to fix page UAF (CVE-2026-98116)\n  * kernel: smb: client: validate absolute native symlink targets before NT fixups (CVE-2026-98318)\n  * kernel: ipv4: validate checksum_start before completing checksum (CVE-2026-99999)\n  * kernel: net/sched: act_ct: fix helper UAF due to extensions realloc (CVE-2026-98442)\n  * kernel: ALSA: ua101: reject mismatched capture/playback packet sizes (CVE-2026-98741)\n  * kernel: net/smc: protect clcsock lifetime in smc_getname (CVE-2026-99032)\n  * kernel: kernel: Denial of Service via unvalidated task in iSCSI management responses (CVE-2026-99152)\n  * kernel: kernel: Denial of service via unvalidated task tag in iSCSI Reject PDU (CVE-2026-99153)\n\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):  \n\n  * [AlmaLinux9.9z] watchdog: System panics during reboot when pretimeout is disabled (0) (JIRA:RHEL-255218)\n  * RT scheduler livelock: migrate-disabled task at pushable-list head causes repeated RT push/stopper retries, starving a critical RT task (remaining issue after CVE-2026-45919 fix in 94894c9c477e) [rhel-9.9.z] (JIRA:RHEL-256280)\n  * MADVISE i/o size in AlmaLinux 9 additionally limited by read_ahead_kb - Was addressed in AlmaLinux8 via RHEL-22476 [rhel-9.9.z] (JIRA:RHEL-259532)\n  * try_charge_memcg() refactor in kernel 5.14.0-687.36.1 causes premature memcg OOM with GiB of clean page cache present [rhel-9.9.z] (JIRA:RHEL-269061)\n  * AlmaLinux9.4 - kernel: CPU hotplug unsupported by CPUMF [rhel-9.9.z] (JIRA:RHEL-270893)\n  * Accel-DSA: dmaengine: idxd: kernel oops on unbind [rhel-9.9.z] (JIRA:RHEL-274411)\n  * af_unix: Fix peek then tail dereference UAF in unix_stream_data_wait() [rhel-9.9] (JIRA:RHEL-275410)\n  * Kernel panic after stopping retis capture [rhel-9.9.z] (JIRA:RHEL-275457)\n  * Hard lockup experienced with repro from RHEL-282072 [rhel-9.9.z] (JIRA:RHEL-290031)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n",
